      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Lectin-induced aggregation of neutrophilic granulocytes was studied in patients with unstable angina pectoris. PHA-P, WGA, ConA, LCL, PHA-L, PHA-E, PSL, HPL, and LABA were used as aggregation inductors. The results indicate restructuring of carbohydrate determinants of glycoprotein receptors in neutrophilic granulocytes which stimulates their aggregation."},
